      "analytical_usefulness": 0.9,
      "source_groundedness": 0.85,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Provides a strong categorical axis to group and compare companies for market-expansion analysis. Values are sound readings of the descriptions (Venture Capital, Professional Services, Enterprise Software all warranted). '23andme' as Healthcare is defensible from its ancestry/health text. Minor risk that some categorisations are inferred beyond the sparse text, but overall well grounded."
    },
    {
      "name": "Geographic_Region",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.7,
      "source_groundedness": 0.6,
      "hallucination_observed": true,
      "rationale": "Regional grouping is a legitimate axis for market-expansion study. However the table already has City/Latitude/Longitude, so it is somewhat redundant, and the specific labels (Silicon Valley vs Peninsula vs Bay Area) require geographic inference from addresses that only give a street. Distinguishing 'Peninsula' from 'Silicon Valley' from a bare street address asserts specificity the source rows do not clearly support."
    },
    {
      "name": "Market_Expansion_Stage",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.85,
      "source_groundedness": 0.35,
      "hallucination_observed": true,
      "rationale": "Directly on-topic for the query and offers a valuable grouping axis. But the values are largely unsupported by the source text: nothing in the descriptions indicates a firm is 'Established', 'Mid-Market', or 'Growth Stage'. Assigning 23andme 'Established' or 280 Group 'Mid-Market' are confident specifics the text is silent on, indicating invented staging labels."
    }
  ],
  "analytical_usefulness": 0.85,
  "source_groundedness": 0.55,
  "rationale": "All three columns give genuine grouping axes directly relevant to studying market-expansion focus, so analytical usefulness is high. Groundedness is mixed: Industry_Focus is well-supported by the descriptions, but Geographic_Region over-specifies region from bare street addresses, and Market_Expansion_Stage asserts stage/maturity labels that the source text provides no basis for, constituting hallucinated specificity."
}

